erns) when generating code with AI. There are no executable commands, network calls, file system operations, or prompt injection attempts targeting the OpenClaw agent itself. The `_meta.json` is standard, and the `SKILL.md` metadata indicates no external binaries are required. The content is purely informational and educational, posing no direct threat.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779164618934},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":4,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789070355402},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a markdown-only educational skill about using AI coding tools, with one loose autonomy tip but no hidden execution, data access, or persistence behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill does not request environment access; references to files, tokens, auth, payments, and APIs are examples for prompting and review workflows rather than instructions to collect or modify sensitive data automatically.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The package contains only markdown files, metadata declares no required binaries, and no install scripts, dependencies, remote fetches, or executable payloads were present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The guidance includes a broad Claude Code tip to let it run for autonomy, but the surrounding materials repeatedly advise planning, approval, testing, and extra review for auth, payments, permissions, and user data.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"It recommends user-managed rules files such as CLAUDE.md and .cursorrules for persistent project context, but this is disclosed, purpose-aligned, and not hidden system persistence or privilege escalation.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is guidance for vibe coding, prompting, workflow, rules files, pitfalls, and tool choice; the artifacts match that purpose and contain no executable code.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Installers should treat this as general advice, not a license to delegate sensitive work blindly. Use the workflow sections that call for reviewing plans, checking diffs, testing changes, and manually scrutinizing auth, payments, permissions, schemas, secrets, and user data handling.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The cited autonomy phrase is real and should be read with caution, but it is a low-impact wording issue in a broader educational guide that also requires plan review, stepwise implementation, testing, and security-sensitive intervention.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789070355402}}}}}